    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d10">

                <pb facs="0085" n="9" sameAs="frus:frus1935v02/pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.4731/112: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Sydney</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Caldwell</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Sydney</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1935-01-08T12:00:00+10:00">January 8,
                        1935—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 8—2:29 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Department’s telegram of June 13, 3 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d10-f1"/> Under
                    instructions of Prime Minister now attending Cabinet meeting in Melbourne, his
                    Secretary today telephoned from Canberra inquiring whether I had received the
                    Department’s reply to the Australian trade proposal and requested me to
                    ascertain for telegraphic information as to probable date of receipt which he
                    hoped might be in the very near future as Cabinet is now considering such
                    matters.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caldwell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
